"Point the camera at an Acorn record-sharing or presentation code, Clear token, NUT-18 Clear "
"payment request, Lightning address or invoice, or GS1 Digital Link, OpenETR evidence link, or "
"HTTPS website address. Scanning only acquires the request; OakGate determines the capability from"
" the code before showing the next action."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/scan_lightning_address.html:32
msgid ""
"The camera starts automatically. If access is unavailable, check the browser's camera permission "
"or enter the code manually. Camera access from another device requires OakGate to be served over "
"HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/scan_lightning_address.html:33
msgid ""
"Once text is acquired, the camera stops. Recognized GS1 Digital Links open OakGate’s independent "
"product verification page, without visiting the printed website. Other HTTPS websites require a "
"warning and confirmation before opening. Receipt/Lightning addresses, valid LNURLs encoding "
"supported Lightning-address endpoints, and Clear payment requests open payment review "
"automatically; payment still requires confirmation. Other codes go to a separate interpretation "
"page. EAN, UPC and DataMatrix camera decoding depends on browser support. Preserve ASCII group "
"separators when pasting GS1 element strings."
msgstr ""

